    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary is correct. The square root must be computed first, requiring $x\\ge0$, so the domain is $[0,\\infty)$.",
      "worked": "Mary is correct. The inner square root must be evaluated first, which requires $x\\ge0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=(\\sqrt{x})^2\\\\f(x)&=x,\\qquad x\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression is undefined for $x<0$, so its domain remains $[0,\\infty)$ after simplification.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
